# PLAYTHORN DREAM 100 — ROUND 2

> Research Date: August 13, 2026 | Evidence-based from live web research
> Methodology: USER VALUE FIRST. Acquisition difficulty scored separately.

---

## ROUND 1 ERROR CORRECTIONS

| Title | Round 1 Claim | CORRECTED Status | Evidence |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Subway Surfers** | "NO official web version → RED" | **WRONG.** SYBO has an OFFICIAL PARTNERSHIP with Poki. Subway Surfers IS officially playable in browser via Poki. SYBO CEO publicly confirmed. Spin-offs Subway Surfers Blast & Match also on Poki. | VERIFIED: GamesBeat, PocketGamer.biz, poki.com |
| **Temple Run 2** | "NO official web version → RED" | **WRONG.** Imangi Studios officially released a web version on Poki in November 2020. This is an authorized distribution. | VERIFIED: Wikipedia, poki.com |
| **Geometry Dash** | "NO official web version → RED" | **PARTIALLY WRONG.** RobTop launched an official web demo at geometrydash.com. Third-party browser ports also exist on CrazyGames. | VERIFIED: geometrydash.com, YouTube |
| **Angry Birds** | "Limited web availability" | **CORRECTED.** Rovio has an official HTML5 web version — Angry Birds Friends — playable via Red's Club (redsclub.com). | VERIFIED: rovio.com, GamesBeat |
| **Kingdom Rush** | "VERIFIED browser version" (vague) | **CORRECTED with specifics.** Available on CrazyGames, Armor Games, Kongregate via Ruffle emulation. Ironhide does NOT host browser version themselves. | VERIFIED: CrazyGames, ArmorGames |
| **Bloons TD 5** | "VERIFIED browser version" (vague) | **CORRECTED.** No official browser version of modern Bloons games. Classic Bloons TD 1-5 available via Ninja Kiwi Archive (desktop app), or unauthorized Ruffle ports on third-party sites. BTD6 has NO browser version. | VERIFIED: ninjakiwi.com |
| **RuneScape** | Listed as browser game | **CORRECTED.** OSRS/RuneScape NO LONGER playable in browser. Requires dedicated client. Browser era ended years ago. | VERIFIED: runescape.com, Reddit |

### New discoveries from Round 2 research:
- **Wordle/NYT Games**: 4-12M daily active users — THE most played browser game by DAU
- **GeoGuessr**: Massive competitive scene (363K peak viewers at World Championship), subscription-based
- **PokeRogue**: Viral Pokémon fan roguelite, browser-native, massive community
- **Poki distribution model**: Default 5-year web exclusivity, 50/50 revenue share (Poki traffic), 100% (dev traffic)

---

## SCORING MODEL

### User Value Score /100 (NO acquisition weighting)

| Component | Weight |
|---|---|
| Gameplay quality & depth | 25% |
| Retention / Replayability | 20% |
| Visual / Presentation quality | 15% |
| Polish / UX | 10% |
| Performance / Browser experience | 10% |
| Popularity / Demand signal | 10% |
| Originality / Differentiation | 10% |

### Acquisition Difficulty /100 (Higher = Harder)

0-20 Very Easy | 21-40 Easy | 41-60 Moderate | 61-80 Difficult | 81-100 Very Difficult

### Strategic Value /100

Combines user demand, quality, retention, differentiation, brand impact, genre importance, repeat-visit potential.

